-- title:
--   Unipotent-fixed vectors vanish when no map to a principal series exists
-- statement:
--   Fix $M\ge 1$ and a weight-two cusp form $g$ on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform, i.e. $g$ is a normalised eigenform (its $q$-coefficient at $1$ is $1$, the coefficients are multiplicative on coprime indices, and satisfy the Hecke recursions $a_{p^{r+2}}=a_pa_{p^{r+1}}-p\,a_{p^r}$ for $p\nmid M$ and $a_{p^{r+2}}=a_pa_{p^{r+1}}$ for $p\mid M$) and no proper divisor of $M$ carries a normalised eigenform whose coefficients at primes not dividing $M$ agree with those of $g$. Let $q$ be a prime and let $\Phi$ be a complex-valued function on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$ which is an adelic lift of $g$: left invariant under the global points $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q})$, right invariant under the finite level-one subgroup attached to the ideal $(M)$, and equal, at adelic points with trivial finite part and archimedean part of positive determinant, to $(g\mid_2 h_\infty)(i)$. Assume further that for all characters $\mu_1,\mu_2\colon\mathbb{Q}_q^\times\to\mathbb{C}^\times$ every $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$-equivariant $\mathbb{C}$-linear map from [`LocalNewvector.AdelicSpan`](def/LocalNewvector_AdelicSpanCarrier.html#L82) $\Phi$ to the principal series carrier [`LocalNewvector.PSCarrier`](def/LocalNewvector_PrincipalSeriesCarrier.html#L173) $q\,\mu_1\,\mu_2$ vanishes. Let $V$ be a complex vector space with a $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$-action by linear maps commuting with the scalars, such that the submodule of vectors fixed by the congruence subgroup of those $x\in\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$ with all entries of $x-1$ and of $x^{-1}-1$ of $q$-adic norm $\le q^{-1}$ is finite-dimensional, and let $f\colon V\to$ [`LocalNewvector.AdelicSpan`](def/LocalNewvector_AdelicSpanCarrier.html#L82) $\Phi$ be an injective equivariant $\mathbb{C}$-linear map whose range is the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$-translates of the distinguished element [`LocalNewvector.AdelicSpan.self`](def/LocalNewvector_AdelicSpanCarrier.html#L121) $\Phi$. Then any vector $v$ of that fixed submodule which is fixed, under the representation [`LocalNewvector.gl2ReductionRep`](def/LocalNewvector_ReductionFunctor.html#L187) $q\,V$ of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/q)$, by all the matrices $\begin{pmatrix}1&t\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$ with $t\in\mathbb{Z}/q$, is zero.
--
--   This is the cuspidality criterion for the $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/q)$-representation on the congruence-fixed vectors of a realisation $V$ of the local representation generated by an adelic lift: no nonzero vector is fixed by the whole upper unipotent subgroup. It feeds the theorems that exhibit a cuspidal type for the local component at $q$, and the related statements producing nonzero maps to principal series under conditions on the inertial characteristic polynomial.
